# CORRECTED (OPS-4 follow-up, F2). The previous 'exempt' rationale here was factually
# wrong and is what let a live break reach production: it enumerated only the
# CONTROL-plane tables this file writes directly in SQL (accounts, users,
# account_members, org_revocations, org_membership_tombstones, user_account_prefs)
# and omitted its TWO `Store::create_graph` calls (`ensure_personal_account`'s
# "Primary" ocean and `ensure_org_account`'s org ocean). `graphs` IS on 0083's
# roster, so post-OPS-4 those INSERTs raised and every brand-new user's first
# authenticated request failed before they ever got an account. Both now run
# through `create_graph_scoped` inside `tenancy::scope::begin_account_scoped` on
# the just-committed account — see `create_first_ocean_scoped`'s doc comment for
# why scoping to a freshly-created account is well-defined (0083's `graphs`
# policy compares the new row's own account_id to the GUC; it never joins
# accounts/account_members, so there is no ordering dependency to satisfy).
# Everything else in this file remains CONTROL-plane and correctly unscoped.
